@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Proposed entity design for the full Part 2 specification
top to bottom direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class TodoList {
  - items: List<TodoItem>
  + addItem(title: String, description: String, dueDate: LocalDate, priority: Priority): void
  + removeItem(index: int): void
  + updateItem(index: int, title: String, description: String, dueDate: LocalDate, priority: Priority): void
  + markCompleted(index: int): void
  + markIncomplete(index: int): void
  + getItem(index: int): TodoItem
  + getSize(): int
  + filterIncomplete(): List<TodoItem>
  + sortBy(key: SortKey): void
}

class TodoItem {
  - title: String
  - description: String
  - dueDate: LocalDate
  - priority: Priority
  - completed: boolean
  + TodoItem(title: String, description: String, dueDate: LocalDate, priority: Priority)
  + edit(title: String, description: String, dueDate: LocalDate, priority: Priority): void
  + markCompleted(): void
  + markIncomplete(): void
  + getTitle(): String
  + getDescription(): String
  + getDueDate(): LocalDate
  + getPriority(): Priority
  + isCompleted(): boolean
}

enum Priority {
  LOW
  MEDIUM
  HIGH
}

enum SortKey {
  NAME
  DUE_DATE
  PRIORITY
}

TodoList "1" *-- "0..*" TodoItem : contains
TodoItem --> Priority
TodoList ..> SortKey

note bottom of TodoList
  UI and persistence are outside this entity diagram.
  Auto-save is an application/persistence responsibility.
  Indexes refer to the current full list. A future filtered UI
  must map its selected task back to that list before editing.
end note
@enduml
